From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: add sensor properties for the GC2145

The PinePhone front camera is a GalaxyCore GC2145 and libcamera has no
entry for it, so every start logs

  WARN CameraSensorProperties camera_sensor_properties.cpp:548
       No static properties available for 'gc2145'
  WARN CameraSensorProperties camera_sensor_properties.cpp:550
       Please consider updating the camera sensor properties database
  WARN CameraSensor camera_sensor_legacy.cpp:502 'gc2145 3-003c':
       No sensor delays found in static properties. Assuming unverified defaults.

and the sensor's physical size is unknown, so nothing can turn the crop
rectangle into a field of view.

The numbers come from the kernel driver rather than a datasheet reading:

  drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
    /* the pixel pitch, in nanometres */
    static const struct v4l2_area gc2145_cell_size = {
            .width = 1750, .height = 1750,
    };

and the test pattern menu it registers, whose value 2 is the full
resolution colour bars (value 1 is the VGA ones, and the rest are skin map
and solid colours that have no libcamera equivalent).

Delays are left empty, as they are for the ov5640 on the same board: this
is a parallel sensor behind sun6i-csi with no documented pipeline depth,
and guessing would be worse than the default.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
@@ -132,6 +132,14 @@
 				.hblankDelay = 2
 			},
 		} },
+		{ "gc2145", {
+			.unitCellSize = { 1750, 1750 },
+			.testPatternModes = {
+				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModeOff, 0 },
+				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModeColorBars, 2 },
+			},
+			.sensorDelays = { },
+		} },
 		{ "hi846", {
 			.unitCellSize = { 1120, 1120 },
 			.testPatternModes = {
